    "description": "Lot of 5 Vintage Glass Electrical Insulators Hemingray Blue Green Clear\nThis lot includes 5 vintage glass electrical insulators featuring both aqua/blue-green and clear glass varieties. Two blue-green insulators are marked with 'HEMINGRAY' and 'MADE IN U.S.A.'. Each insulator is made of heavy, thick glass with a classic double-groove design. Most pieces exhibit signs of age including minor dirt, residue, and surface wear but have no major cracks or chips visible. The clear glass insulators include one with a partial label and some with embossed markings. These insulators were originally used on telegraph and power lines and are suitable for collectors or as decorative industrial items.\n9 x 8 x 4 in\nDetails\nLocal Pickup is now available.\nPlease initiate all scheduling, inquiries and notifications via your Shopgoodwill account by selecting: Contact Us then Create a New Support ticket.\nPlease make sure to read description, look at all pics and ask questions prior to bidding as all sales are final.\nGeneral Conditions\nAll items are used, sold as found, and AS IS with no warranties expressed or implied.\nWe are not experts in any field; descriptions are based on our best ability using available resources.\nMeasurements are approximate.\nPlease read the description, review all images, and ask questions prior to bidding. All sales are final.\nPlacing a bid indicates acceptance of these terms.\nJewelry & Precious Metals\nWe do not have a gemologist or jeweler on staff. Items are listed to the best of our ability and have not been professionally tested or serviced.\nDiamonds vs. moissanite cannot be differentiated by our equipment.\nGems are tested with a Presidium Gem Tester; however, it cannot distinguish natural vs. synthetic stones, and items may have flaws, scratches, or inclusions beyond our ability to identify.\nGold-filled items are only described as marked/stamped or by magnetic properties. Actual karat levels may vary.\nMagnetic clasps may be present in precious metal jewelry due to spring mechanisms.\nJewelry testing is only performed upon request, using acid testing. Any post-purchase testing is the buyer’s responsibility, and refunds will not be issued based on authenticity disputes.\nDesigner items are not authenticated unless specifically stated.\nWatches may not include batteries; functionality is not guaranteed.\nLot Listings\nLots may contain mixed items (e.g., jewelry, watches, coins, toys, sports/trading cards, marbles, Legos, etc.).\nItems in lots may be unsorted and can include broken, dirty, tangled, or incomplete pieces. Stones, beads, or parts may be missing.\nDue to volume, we cannot answer detailed questions about individual pieces within a lot.\nLots are non-refundable and cannot be combined with other purchases.\nAuthentication\nSignatures and autographs are not authenticated unless specified.\nName brand items are not authenticated unless listed as Certified Authentic.\nCertified items are authenticated through AuthenticateFirst.com and include a certificate in compliance with ShopGoodwill’s brand policy.\nElectronics & Clocks\nTested only for powering on, unless otherwise stated.\nFurther testing is performed only if equipment is available, and results will be noted in the listing.\nItems sold AS IS, with no refunds on functionality.",
